## 5. R8 CODE SHRINKING AND OBFUSCATION (release builds only)

- Install `expo-build-properties` with `npx expo install expo-build-properties` (if it's not already installed).
- In `app.json`, add or update the plugin config:
  ```json
  [
    "expo-build-properties",
    {
      "android": {
        "enableProguardInReleaseBuilds": true,
        "enableShrinkResourcesInReleaseBuilds": true
      }
    }
  ]
  ```
- Keep any existing plugin entries (AdMob, the document scanner, the image picker, and so on) unchanged.
- Do NOT enable these for development builds. They only apply to release builds.
- R8 can strip code that native libraries load by name. Do not guess at rules. If a production build crashes at launch or during scanning, ads, or OCR, report the exact crash log. The fix will be a targeted `proguard-rules.pro` keep rule, added only for the library that breaks.

